Status: IN_PROGRESS
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/BowserBoy/issues/86
Milestone: Native touchscreen marks align with the pointer and ordinary taps register.
Dependencies: 79 separate DS; 87 independent DS gameplay orientation.
Purpose: Correct the reported Twin Lab stylus offset without distorting input
for other games or weakening screen/lid visibility checks.

Tasks:
- [x] Reproduce the discrepancy in native output and trace coordinates end to end.
- [x] Correct the cause rather than applying a compensating host-screen offset.
- [x] Verify new native marks at clicked pixels across body/hinge/zoom changes.
- [x] Cover LCD edges, upside-down pose, resizing and high-DPI touch input.
- [x] Reproduce lost quick taps and preserve contact edges across actual native frames.
- [x] Coalesce drag moves and cancel queued contacts on input/lifecycle changes.
- [x] Qualify quick mouse/touch taps and existing native/pen lifecycle together.
- [x] Update affected documentation, contributor context and GitHub tracking.
- [ ] Owner visual review.

Acceptance criteria:
The actual native lower framebuffer draws at each clicked LCD pixel, not merely
somewhere on the screen. Physical UVs retain their original mapping in any
visible orientation. Mouse/touch coordinates remain accurate across zoom,
resizing and device-pixel ratios. Upper LCDs, hidden/covered/back-facing surfaces
and points outside the LCD do not become touchscreen targets. GBA behavior,
unrelated DS ROM bytes, pose locks and save formats remain unchanged.
Ordinary short mouse/touch taps work without artificially holding contact.
Queued drag moves do not build a stale backlog; cancellation discards pending
contacts rather than replaying them after blur, pause, tools or console changes.

Completion evidence:
Responsiveness follow-up: owner rejects localhost Twin Lab touch response and
reports lag. All eight ordinary clicks reproduce missing native and copied-LCD
marks despite correct host/native coordinates and current served ROM bytes.
Native down/up events arrive only0-0.3ms apart. The earlier twelve-point
precision fixture holds contact and therefore does not qualify quick taps.
A new genuine quick-click regression fails before the timing fix.
Two browser RAFs still lose touches; the pinned getFrameNum counter proves
browser paints are not native input-poll boundaries. Preserve down/up across
actual native frame changes, coalesce only pending moves, preserve contact
starts/endpoints and clear queued input on cancellation/lifecycle changes.
The first native quick-tap gate passes30.7s with/without the held pen.
Expanded twelve-contact mouse/touch case passes17.5s, including picked-up pen,
upside-down390x844DPR2, naturally copied pixels and native edge-frame ordering.
Final integrated Edge gate passes10cases/4.5m: physical DS input/occlusion,
backup restore, dual-core isolation/cold power, nondefault checkpoint reload,
four-pose precision, quick taps, hinge controls, branding and GBA quick actions.
The earlier separate held-pen lifecycle also passes25.8s. All43units,
syntax/build pass. Hosted publication remains a separate monitored gate.

The regression fails before the fix at native (200,150) in flat gameplay.
Final35units,syntax/build and both affected native Edge cases pass together1.6m
(50.7s lifecycle,41.7s precision). Twelve fresh native yellow-pixel targets and
actual physical-LCD probes cover four locked body/hinge poses, upside-down,
exact corners, held mouse/touch drags,50/65%zoom and390x844DPR2 resizing.
Brush count remains64 with origins within one native pixel of pointer rounding;
physical antialiased corners use a3x3drawing-buffer footprint.
Captured stylus and host focus remain held; genuine blur releases them.
Companion native case retains lid occlusion, buttons, backups, power/reload
and inactive-GBA isolation. Actual rolled/phone captures reviewed.
Owner/device review remains pending; no full-suite or deployment claim.
Scoped synchronization verifies issue86 OPEN, Project1/In progress and backlink.

